      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose of 3200 mg. Single doses are normally capped at 800 mg. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a high risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention.\n\nIt may be a transcription or unit error, or a different intended regimen. For example, 400 mg four times daily is 1600 mg per day, or 800 mg three times daily is 2400 mg per day. Please check with the prescribing physician.\n\nAlso, medication orders for patients need to come from a licensed prescriber on the medicine team. If you're involved in this patient's care, please route the order through the attending or the pharmacy team. If you tell me the intended dose and frequency and confirm that a prescriber has approved it, I can enter it. Please note the prescriber's name in the order note."
      }
